                              "fill": "#d9cac1",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "height": 60.88,
                              "content": "Instead of writing the classification logic ourselves, we give a neural network the same 30 machines the rules were tested on, with their known outcomes. Backpropagation (1986) pushes the error backwards through the hidden layers and nudges every weight — and the hidden neurons learn to bend the boundary where a fixed threshold can't.",
